# GM2 voice banks for models without GM2 voices of their own (issue #34)
# Bank select MSB 121 + LSB 0-9 (GM2 capital and variation tones). Yamaha's own S-YXG50 table (sxgbin41.tbl)
# has these ten banks; they hold no voices of their own but point at XG and GS voices. This is that list of
# positions only, no voice data: one row per GM2 LSB (0-9), one token per program (0-127):
#   X<n>       XG bank MSB 0 / LSB n, same program
#   X<n>:<p>   XG bank MSB 0 / LSB n, program p (one entry: GM2 LSB 2, program 39 -> XG LSB 66, program 38)
#   G<n>       GS bank MSB n, same program (the sound effects 120-127)
# makeSYXG50 builds the GM2 banks from the converted model's own banks; a position the model does not have
# falls back to its capital tone like any XG bank select (XG LSB row) or, for GS, to XG LSB 0.
# GM2 drum kits (MSB 120) take the GS kit assignment of the drum programs.
